priority: -2
new-page: true
tags: event
face-image: img/Jozef-Pilsudski-Polish-soldiers.webp
on-arrival: {!
for (var party of Q.parties) {
    Q[party + '_pres_votes'] = Math.round(((Q[party + '_sj'] + Q[party + '_sn']) / 2) * 10) / 10;
}

Q.narutowicz_votes = 0;
Q.daszynski_votes = 0;
Q.wojciechowski_votes = 0;
Q.courtenay_votes = 0;
Q.zamoyski_votes = 0;

Q.narutowicz_dropped = 0;
Q.daszynski_dropped = 0;
Q.wojciechowski_round = 0;
Q.courtenay_round = 0;
Q.zamoyski_round = 0;

Q.round = 1;

Q.endorsement_daszynski = 0;
Q.psl_l_choice = 'Narutowicz';
Q.psl_w_choice = 'Narutowicz';
Q.psl_p_choice = 'Wojciechowski';
Q.npr_choice = 'Wojciechowski';
Q.pps_choice = '0';
Q.kpp_choice = '0';
Q.bmn_choice = 'Courtenay';
Q.other_choice = 'Courtenay';
Q.chzjn_choice = 'Zamoyski';

!}

=  1922 Presidential Election

Its time to view the candidates. Now, Piłsudski is expected to run after calls for him to contend from moderates, <span style="color: #c00000;">socialists</span>, and even some right-wing followers- wait, what? Piłsudski isnt running? 

It seems that Marshal Piłsudski has decided not to run for the presidential election due to the constitution limiting the powers of the head of state, instead, he will attempt to rally the **<span style="color: #CCC;">Pol</span><span style="color: #DC143C;">ish</span>** parties  towards a unity candidate he supports.

After his decision to not run as a candidate, many parties have been left scrambling to put forward a candidate that is **not** Piłsudski, due to this decision coming close to the presidential elections.

- @who

@who
title: Who will be the successor of Piłsudski?
subtitle: Good question.

Without a unifying figure such as Piłsudski around, many fear the ChZJN might win the presidency, however, Piłsudski must have a plan, right? He wouldnt have dropped out without having a plan.

Now, from all these possible candidates, Piłsudski's first choice is..

- @witos

@witos
title: Witos Wincenty.
face-image: img/portraits/WitosWincenty.jpeg

Witos Wincenty, former Prime Minister, a moderate and leader of the PSL-P, has been suggested as a unity candidate against the ChZJN by Piłsudski, however he has declined the candidacy, and Piłsudski starts searching for someone else. Now, who is second on his list..

- @narutowicz

@narutowicz
title: Gabriel Narutowicz.
face-image: img/Narutowicz_Pilsudski.jpg

Piłsudski talks with Gabriel Narutowitcz, a friend of his and former Public Works and Foreign minister, to discuss his candidacy agaisnt the ChZJN, after Wicenty refused to take the candidacy.

Piłsudski attempts to convince Narutowicz...

- @narutoyay
  
@narutoyay
title: Narutowicz accepts!
face-image: img/portraits/NarutowiczGabriel.jpg
on-arrival: narutowicz_votes = (psl_l_pres_votes + psl_w_pres_votes)

With Narutowicz nominated to replace Piłsudski, can he expect the moderates throw their support behind him, especially due to some moderates looking at him as a puppet or tool of Piłsudski?

For better or worse, Narutowicz did not secure the support of the moderates, However his candidacy is still supported by the PSL-L and PSL-W.

- @candidate

@candidate
title: What other candidates will be present in the <span class="wide_tooltip-wrap">campaign trail<span class="wide_tooltip-tip"><img src="img/campaign_trail.webp">good game</span></span>?

- @zamoyski
- @courtenay
- @wojciechowski
- @communist

@zamoyski
title: Maurycy Zamoyski.
subtitle: A non-partisan candidate fielded by the ChZJN. Largest estate and the biggest land owner. Serving as the **<span style="color: #CCC;">Pol</span><span style="color: #DC143C;">ish</span>** envoy to **<span style="color: #000091;">Pa</span><span style="color: #CCC;">r</span><span style="color: #E1000F;">is</span>**.
on-arrival: candidate += 1; zamoyski_votes = (zln_pres_votes + pschd_pres_votes + otherright_pres_votes)
go-to: candidate
max-visits: 1
face-image: img/portraits/ZamoyskiMaurycy.jpg

Maurycy Zamoyski, one of **<span style="color: #CCC;">Pol</span><span style="color: #DC143C;">and</span>**'s wealthiest landowners and its envoy to **<span style="color: #000091;">Pa</span><span style="color: #CCC;">r</span><span style="color: #E1000F;">is</span>** is the chosen candidate of the ChZJN. His nationalist and aristocratic background, combined with his experience in foreign affairs as part of the **<span style="color: #CCC;">Pol</span><span style="color: #DC143C;">ish</span>** delegation to the **Paris Conference**, which concluded with the signing of the **Treaty of Versailles**, makes him the preferred candidate of the ChZJN.

His candidacy is supported by the ChZJN.

@courtenay
title: Jan Baudouin de Courtenay.
subtitle: **<span style="color: #CCC;">Pol</span><span style="color: #DC143C;">ish</span>** and <span style="color: #CCC;">**Ru**</span><span style="color: #0036A7;">**ssi**</span><span style="color: #D62718;">**an**</span> Linguist and a staunch supporter for Minority rights.
on-arrival: candidate += 1; courtenay_votes = (bmn_pres_votes + other_pres_votes)
go-to: candidate
max-visits: 1
face-image: img/portraits/CourtenayJan.jpg

Jan Baudouin de Courtenay is a relatively obscure candidate, known for his theory of Phoneme. His candidacy was proposed by the BMN due to him being a strong supporter of the national revival of various national minority and ethnic groups, taking a relatively pro-minority stance.

Even though Courtenay isn't expected to win, His candidacy is supported by the BMN and the other minority parties as a show of solidarity against right-wing dominance.

@wojciechowski
title: Stanisław Wojciechowski.
subtitle: A Moderate member of the PSL-P, former Interior Minister
on-arrival: candidate += 1; wojciechowski_votes = (npr_pres_votes + psl_p_pres_votes)
go-to: candidate
max-visits: 1
face-image: img/portraits/WojciechowskiStanisław.jpg

Witos Wincenty has been a bit unpopular with the more moderate wings of the PSL-P, primarily due to his right-wing tendencies and his neglect of attention to the rural villages.  Hence, Stanisław Wojciechowski, who is also a former Interior Minister serving from 1919 to 1920 has been fielded as a compromise candidate representing the Centrist and Moderates of the PSL-P. Interestingly enough, he was previously a member of our party.

His candidacy is supported by the PSL-P and NPR.

@communist
title: How about the Communists?
view-if: candidate >= 3

The KPP *as expected* has decided to boycott the presidential election.

- @pps

@pps
title: So, what is our decision? Should we run our own candidate?

- @daszynskielection: Run <span style="color: #C62828;">Ignacy Daszyński</span> of the PPS.
- @narutowiczelection: Support Narutowicz as a unity candidate.
- @wojciechowskielection: Support <span style="color: #3A6538;">Wojciechowski</span> of the PSL-P.

@daszynskielection
subtitle: This is the default choice 
on-arrival: pps_choice = 'Daszynski'; daszynski_votes = pps_pres_votes
face-image: img/portraits/DaszyńskiIgnacy.jpg

We have chosen to field <span class="wide_tooltip-wrap">Ignacy Dasyznski<span class="wide_tooltip-tip"><img src="img/portraits/DaszyńskiIgnacy.jpg"> Leader of the PPS </span></span>.

